{"title":"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5(CHEAP)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5(CHEAP)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53c3302151c8bc9e98ed3dc304935aded998ede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin t + i \\cos t)^n = \\sin nt + i \\cos nt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"18\" /> true for all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Moivre%27s_Theorem\" title=\"De Moivre&#39;s Theorem\">De Moivre's Theorem</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d779777e588edd08f0c72c749101de3c9ca60c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\cos t + i \\sin t)^n = \\cos nt + i \\sin nt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"18\" /> for all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> and all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  So, we'd like to somehow convert our given expression into a form from which we can apply De Moivre's Theorem.  \n</p><p>Recall the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\">trigonometric identities</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb33a7d0137b410d9cc2beb28a74bed0b79f3823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\left(\\frac{\\pi}2 - u\\right) = \\sin u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"156\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4df9888de207c3f68b017453624911e710d7c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}2 - u\\right) = \\cos u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"156\" height=\"33\" /> hold for all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  If our original equation holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, it must certainly hold for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d533254cc7485d992139531f8869960041123da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\frac{\\pi}2 - u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"33\" />.  Thus, the question is equivalent to asking for how many <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65892495b840856fc9bf7983f01396371710123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3901c1f44a9c8dab5894298ed8f35be780c0ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi2 - u\\right) + i \\cos\\left(\\frac\\pi 2 - u\\right)\\right)^n = \\sin n \\left(\\frac\\pi2 -u \\right) + i\\cos n \\left(\\frac\\pi2 - u\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"523\" height=\"34\" /> holds for all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba1d700927bca7df8c8f988dcaf591506be783c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi2 - u\\right) + i \\cos\\left(\\frac\\pi 2 - u\\right)\\right)^n = \\left(\\cos u + i \\sin u\\right)^n = \\cos nu + i\\sin nu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"555\" height=\"34\" />.  We know that two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_number\" title=\"Complex number\">complex numbers</a> are equal if and only if both their <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_part\" title=\"Real part\">real part</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_part\" title=\"Imaginary part\">imaginary part</a> are equal.  Thus, we need to find all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/5518bd916f8346b9821cadebf01f61d54b9a23d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos n u = \\sin n\\left(\\frac\\pi2 - u\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"178\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5219c72a537569e4ba98f44720e2dea1542989c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin nu = \\cos n\\left(\\frac\\pi2 - u\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"178\" height=\"33\" /> hold for all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43308ce7f7da4aa3eec6bf3e62c4d7890b0f167.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x = \\cos y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" /> if and only if either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8daf68e8cd4d3a30959ebceff93c0335d3246553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = \\frac \\pi 2 + 2\\pi \\cdot k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"33\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd9d3abe6e3d8710991a4f87bc96c412c1bb4d7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - y = \\frac\\pi2 + 2\\pi\\cdot k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"33\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.  So from the equality of the real parts we need either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/834857825340d27b1b1d5c54658673352329a6ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nu + n\\left(\\frac\\pi2 - u\\right) = \\frac\\pi 2 + 2\\pi \\cdot k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"230\" height=\"33\" />, in which case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5cef70cb53013a4982c5d5407e330061e64e36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1 + 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, or we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcd04b87ae4dc1b660dc73d55924ae6498cb8d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-nu + n\\left(\\frac\\pi2 - u\\right) = \\frac\\pi 2 + 2\\pi \\cdot k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"244\" height=\"33\" />, in which case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> will depend on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and so the equation will not hold for all real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  Checking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5cef70cb53013a4982c5d5407e330061e64e36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1 + 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> in the equation for the imaginary parts, we see that it works there as well, so exactly those values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842dac4a51f17d41ec6e1d1a3fc3fb845d8f5f8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> work.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1dcdc80b186e19cbc0115ed7ccf84a43e7963c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> of them in the given range.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>This problem begs us to use the familiar identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acced135011357886c14d07167d5686c95edf196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{it} = \\cos(t) + i \\sin(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"22\" />. Notice, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00ecd903d909493adec2d316fce54b372e80ec2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(t) + i \\cos(t) = i(\\cos(t) - i \\sin(t)) = i e^{-it}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"19\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265159338e4a409d84116c70fed6c559723cc242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(-t) = -\\sin(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />. Using this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c25acd13a14701d932bd13ffd9fa8b31866b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin(t) + i \\cos(t))^n = \\sin(nt) + i \\cos(nt)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"307\" height=\"18\" /> is recast as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5454f97f12ee55b5195d47f21c3dd753d6c566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i e^{-it})^n = i e^{-itn}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"19\" />. Hence we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4276abaf8cff3b7783779c0b9f9067480a0746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^n = i \\Rightarrow i^{n-1} = 1 \\Rightarrow n \\equiv 1 \\bmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"266\" height=\"15\" />. Thus since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> exactly one quarter of the residues are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hence we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1dcdc80b186e19cbc0115ed7ccf84a43e7963c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18aab5c08f621e8e4651e69d83a563d3f7762b03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/879e74186a54507579488657623a1426924301c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-t\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65d5859dd6226d24232ec85a9c5ee32a7312e95b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7d840fb91c6f01ccb3e9a5c7d8df9f2e103566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-t\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"33\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88c1c86e2eacdf0d4d8b7671c7b9d178907d561d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin t + i\\cos t = e^{i\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-t\\right)}=\\frac{e^{\\frac{\\pi i}{2}}}{e^{it}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"227\" height=\"41\" />. This theorem also tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d219df1a4eb2870d207f808c149c12d6a5d2f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{\\frac{\\pi i}{2}}=i$\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a084c39bcaf32dc954c5a4d2ee612771d972e393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin t + i\\cos t = \\frac{i}{e^{it}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"39\" />. By the same line of reasoning, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c679ef1e2fa36b8c9db030f0aefe8b962c00ee91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin nt + i\\cos nt = \\frac{i}{e^{int}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>For the statement in the question to be true, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a6914a936e05c78ac23e0df47ae0ccdb6c26d07a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{i}{e^{it}}\\right)^n=\\frac{i}{e^{int}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"115\" height=\"46\" />. The left hand side simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae77f9709d7bb43cffb2c033b109356c628ed64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{i^n}{e^{int}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />. We cancel the denominators and find that the only thing that needs to be true is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42bfc06ef09a0b90f1eddb5c5f9a86cf78655955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^n=i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />. This is true if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d19e6dfc783f3a66952dbd86e8c0783ed44081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv1\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1dcdc80b186e19cbc0115ed7ccf84a43e7963c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> such numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Solution by Zeroman\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We are using degrees in this solution instead of radians. I just process stuff better that way.\n</p><p>We can see that the LHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b73b8ee1bd68b34e6963384f39ee7226fc542d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cis(n(90^{\\circ}-t))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />, and the RHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a654d5095df49df8f87fb45007da5935c8d3f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cis(90^{\\circ}-nt)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/3/ab397c7d028900e3d860aa6c93976adf9ba7a809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(90-t) \\equiv 90-nt \\mod 360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" /> Expanding and canceling the nt terms, we will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/159d774e20d3c3b1c88296568d99361e5f12defe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90n \\equiv 90 \\mod 360$\" width=\"151\" height=\"12\" />. Canceling gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3405c65f536dd63674245c4fbe706d8c326130bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1 \\mod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />, and thus there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1dcdc80b186e19cbc0115ed7ccf84a43e7963c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> values of n.\n</p><p>-AlexLikeMath\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5.28CHEAP.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5(CHEAP)\">Solution 5(CHEAP)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5(CHEAP)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a607fd61885c014512c949fee18869690330407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=0$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />. Then, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42bfc06ef09a0b90f1eddb5c5f9a86cf78655955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^n=i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b60316060abced4173a0697d5c6509a3c085122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv 1\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1dcdc80b186e19cbc0115ed7ccf84a43e7963c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb57d3bd503fe5ba5b565dc135b7b6a0b706c95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^n$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd52a9a93bc5f514671d0f17d95db21dc9bc44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin t + i \\cos t)^n = i^n (\\cos(t) - i \\sin t)= i^n(\\cos(nt) - i\\sin nt).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"470\" height=\"18\" /> We know the final expression must be the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b4c3a31bcb957e5c5a888955e2465e614f90bcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin nt + i \\cos nt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" /> so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d9bfe4ac4666ab8f53b63a2a455a14c906a56f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^n(\\cos(nt) - i\\sin nt) = \\sin nt + i \\cos nt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" /> in which testing yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77eb0c927773ed1b909a0d12b086879d925df5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> is the only mod that works, so we have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/581e5952911d36ef5e80beb5e2f0f40fac55f5e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 \\cdot\\frac{1}{4} = \\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"37\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that work.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that this looks like de Moivre's except switched around. Using de Moivre's as motivation we try to convert the given expression into de Moivre's. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/9042393c1420f1f229669db4de2c6c3255eac39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin t = \\cos(90 - t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b63ee78bf5d27d5dc29590d0ba65d059beccf43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos t = \\sin(90 - t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />. So we rewrite the expression and setting it equal to the given expression in the problem, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4524d0aff55044355a86f5ef0c76992b087e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(90 - nt) + i\\sin(90 - nt) = \\cos(90n - nt) + i\\sin(90n - nt)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"489\" height=\"18\" />. Now we can just look at the imaginary parts. Doing so and simplifying, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416522d3953eafc4b35e84ccc1cca9b6c74667d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 4k= n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. From this we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/083a12c828894c7030af36c59130afb7f881f659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />. So there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1dcdc80b186e19cbc0115ed7ccf84a43e7963c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> solutions. \n</p><p>~coolmath_2018\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e58de99983e886f9f82438b724cc03688cafc51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin\\theta + i\\cos\\theta)^{n} = i^{n} (\\cos\\theta - i\\sin\\theta)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"292\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Hence the required condition is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/87685f4406c9d3f0b6cd3fbc410eb3da620a410e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{n} = i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> which is true for exactly 1 in 4 consecutive numbers. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1dcdc80b186e19cbc0115ed7ccf84a43e7963c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that this equation is extremely similar to De Moivre's Theorem. If we can find a way to flip the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" />, we'll be good. So we just need to relate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> to each other. Ah-ha! We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e5339070e81cab97576772703cf1e3e2e0bfe385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}=\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"35\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565d765209d6becfd7d4b6d36e1a519ab4d9900e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x}=\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"35\" />. So, substituting gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbc8513e46455efb824c2d230f87940c21f82b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left[\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)}+i\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}-x\\right)}\\right]^n=\\cos{ \\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}-nt\\right)}+i\\sin{ \\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}-nt\\right)}=\\sin{nt}+i\\cos{nt}.\\]\" width=\"657\" height=\"34\" /> Let us compare the real parts since they must be equal (we could also do the same for the imaginary parts, as well). So, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9197708e33afcf57ff241241a97b5073c5e4b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}-nt\\right)}=\\sin{nt}=\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}-nt\\right)}\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"33\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c6090bb2a3e5fdce39cc74f470cf74b1ad8721.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow \\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}-nt=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}-nt+2\\pi{k}, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}.\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"32\" /> Solving, we find, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d77627b9bf74e62381bb72abbde2cafef659254.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{(n-1)\\pi}{2}=2\\pi{k}\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d592213309b11d0abf31767a2c2e3bd0b2daa4b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow n=4k+1\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a0917e282887c3ff31f16a3c3712e757c5e235f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow n=1,5,9,...,997 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{250}.\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II\" title=\"2005 AIME II\">2005 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017110706\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 596/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18860/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.020      1 -total\n 59.27%    7.717      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.78%    5.049      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2548:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017110706 and revision id 290791. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}